{"trans": "Promote fair competition and oppose deceit and suspicion; encourage a diverse online environment; promote cooperation and oppose self-interest; encourage mutual benefit and win-win outcomes online."}
{"trans": "In summary, perhaps more overseas companies believe that listing in the United States is not worth the effort, so they choose to take the high road, but this does not mean they are prepared to abandon the US market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a turbulent market environment, it is extremely difficult for gold to remain unscathed, and discussing the possibility of breaking the $1,000 threshold is likely to be a pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police officer explained that the students' actions were an act of bravery and righteousness. They stepped forward during the elderly man's critical moment of falling into the water, which is very commendable. It was learned that the elderly man had a mild mental illness, and after the hospital's full rescue efforts, he has been stabilized."}
{"trans": "Of course, the above methods are just a few effective ways to revise. There are many ways to organize a revision sprint, and they should be chosen according to the individual characteristics of each candidate. I wish all candidates a successful start and immediate success!"}
{"trans": "The place where Princess Zhaojun dismounted has become another river in this lifetime. The stones of history are still speaking, the grass is still the green flowers of yesteryear, and the cattle and sheep are still humbly burying their heads, not knowing today. In the meticulous passage of time, people drink water and think of their origins, sitting in the fragrance of wine by the autumn waters of Lake Nanshan, the night is smoke-free."}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking to eat well every day or living for a hundred years. One cannot live twice, so how can one fulfill the meaning and value of life before death? Even if one is reduced to ashes, one must leave a resounding echo like a precious stone striking the ground, and radiate the light of life in the world."}
{"trans": "The other people were able to remain calm, holding their guns and observing the enemy from all around, but Li Wenbin was in a panic, diving into the grass with his buttocks up in the air and his hands protecting his head, looking very embarrassed. The people with him covered their faces and laughed, and Li Wenbin's prestige immediately plummeted."}
{"trans": "\"How do you plan to be a king?\" the animals asked, half-believing and half-doubting. \"First, I will resolve disputes impartially and fairly. Second, I will handle state affairs diligently and tirelessly. Third, when facing a strong enemy, I will lead by example and charge forward. This is my governance speech.\""}
{"trans": "He is worldly and experienced, and can change direction like a compass needle. His guiding star is fickle and not fixed. Fortunately, he is good at using sweet-talking words to win people's favor, so he has never suffered any setbacks due to his despicable nature. Moreover, he is eloquent and talkative (unless he is not paid enough)."}
{"trans": "When I first followed my colleague to the stock exchange, I was destined to have an unbreakable bond with stocks. Seventeen springs, summers, autumns, and winters allowed me to experience the ups and downs of the stock market. After going through many ups and downs, I have become a veteran, and the past is still vivid in my mind! 1. The sea of suffering is boundless, but turning back is the right path."}
{"trans": "The defeated soldiers fled for a long time before stopping, and he sighed, \"I have been fighting since I was twenty-five, winning every battle and conquering every fortress, but now in my twilight years, I have suffered such a crushing defeat, it truly drives me to despair!\" The news of the victory in the defense of Ningyuan reached the court, and everyone was overjoyed, raising their cups in celebration."}
{"trans": "On their wedding day, relatives and friends came to offer their congratulations one after another. Since the living room decoration should not be too unconventional, it should be comfortable and welcoming. It should make the couple feel comfortable and make the guests feel at home. Soft fabric sofas and throw pillows are essential elements."}
{"trans": "I said, \"Let's not beat around the bush; let's stick to the facts.\" My son said, \"For years, I've noticed your detached attitude towards computers, and I think you consider them too sacred. You dare not touch this, and you can't move that. The biggest obstacle to learning for mothers like you is treating computers like gods.\""}
{"trans": "He is always on edge, afraid of saying the wrong thing, afraid of doing the wrong thing, afraid of offending others. Throughout his life, Zhi'er often recalls some unfortunate events, which inevitably brings him sadness. As for Zhu, he is always suspicious, always thinking that others are plotting against him, so he is always on guard and often suffers from insomnia."}
{"trans": "In the last shameful corner there is a pitiful guillotine, skulking and frightened, a disgrace, as if always on edge, afraid of being caught in the act of doing something wrong - because every time it finishes its deed, it immediately makes a hasty retreat. How could one not feel relieved by all this?"}
{"trans": "At this point, the true charm of fighting lies in the tense atmosphere before the fight, the heated arguments during the fight, the persuasive words during the mediation, the friendly toasts after the fight, the deep friendship after the fight, and the side-by-side battle in the next fight. This cycle continues, and the ranks of the pacifists grow stronger."}
{"trans": "The baron's blatant insult is truly unbearable; just wait, you shameless fanatic, for the sake of honor, I will take on the responsibility of avenging this insult. Only he can bear the responsibility of avenging this blatant insult by everyone; he cannot swallow his pride even if it means losing his life."}
{"trans": "It seems there will be no quarrel, no storm and thunder, and now everything is calm. However, my mother once again asked an untimely question: \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" My daughter's answer was also strange and untimely: \"Later, dear mom, let's see later.\""}
{"trans": "In terms of interpersonal relationships, he is still at the initial stage, but when it comes to knowledge, he is well-prepared. No matter how eloquent the director is, he may not be more tricky than the professors at the master's thesis defense. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, he may be at a loss, but if you ask him how to chop wood, isn't that a piece of cake?"}
{"trans": "You will soon reap the consequences of your idleness.” After saying this, the ox lowered its head to the yoke and pulled its cart full of fertilizer away. You should live a virtuous life and be mindful throughout your life to avoid laziness and idleness. If you still do not feel ashamed, you will surely reap what you sow."}
{"trans": "Paint it so that it is vivid and lifelike. His art has repeatedly deceived people's eyes, making them mistake it for a real object at first glance, never realizing it was a painting. For hundreds of years, painting art had been considered low-brow and unworthy of high praise, but in his hands, it was once again elevated and flourished."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized, considered sacred and inviolable, mysterious and inscrutable, and thus worshipped as gods. This is why they were called \"Heavenly Kings.\" In reality, emperors were also human, with both good and bad qualities. Among emperors, there were wise rulers who were capable of governing the country and stabilizing the nation, as well as incompetent and tyrannical rulers."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he \"laughed at the sky and went out,\" chanting \"Are we mere commoners?\" The deceit in the officialdom, the hypocrisy of the world, and the cold reality cooled down his passion. How could the golden facade of a \"court poet\" cover your wild and unrestrained heart? Finally, after experiencing the setbacks and pain of the officialdom, you found peace."}
{"trans": "\"A suspicious vagrant has been harassing our territory for some time now, stirring up trouble and causing discord. You must apprehend this troublemaker within the next day and sentence him to death.\" \"We will certainly comply, sir,\" the police said and left. The criminal was one-eyed and did not notice the knowing glances they exchanged when responding."}
{"trans": "Americans have never worshipped their national leaders as gods, nor have they blindly followed their every word. However, Obama succumbed to the expectations of his supporters. He also believed that he was the long-awaited savior they had been waiting for. The people's silence was a wake-up call for him. But the feeling of rapid advancement was so intoxicating that it almost made him forget his original purpose."}
{"trans": "Taurus men, who are usually smiling and down-to-earth, have a practical personality and cannot tolerate betrayal. Don’t try to probe their true feelings; the steady bull is content with grazing and eating grass, smiling at you like Jesus looking at his sheep. If you don’t want to bring the camera to the Spanish bullfighting arena, where blood flows like rivers and the scene is horrific, don’t make him jealous."}
{"trans": "Gemini wouldn't have any fun in life without a little trickery and cleverness. Don't be fooled by his carefree demeanor; once things get complicated, he'll surprise you. While others are fighting to the death, he reaps the benefits. But once he successfully captures everyone's attention, he'll act like a carefree prince and walk away, playing the game of feigning weakness to lure you in."}
{"trans": "In reality, being part of the Eurozone and bound by the euro, it is simply unrealistic for Germany to try to save itself. When the Eurozone was established, the grand vision of shared prosperity was embraced. Now, the Greek debt crisis has triggered a European debt crisis, and it is only natural that one loss affects all. When the city gate catches fire, the fish in the pond suffer. Moreover, the surrounding areas are already in flames, and some places are fast becoming wastelands."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, direct investment in commodities may be the most direct and effective way to combat inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investment, the first thing that comes to mind are often some shocking stories, such as those who went bankrupt by speculating in commodity futures, or airlines that suffered huge losses by hedging crude oil prices, etc. It seems that the risks of commodity investment are so high that ordinary people are deterred."}
{"trans": "The vast sky tolerates the fury of thunder and lightning, and then there is fair weather; the vast ocean tolerates the raging waves, and then there are calm waters; the quiet forest tolerates the cruelty of the survival of the fittest, and then there is the singing of birds and the fragrance of flowers. The sky, the ocean, and the forest, because they understand tolerance, retreat at the right time, and bend down to accept, thus they have beauty and extraordinaryness. When you bend down, the world becomes wider."}
{"trans": "Looking back at the changes in the college entrance examination in recent years, what we need is to firmly grasp the new trends and new developments in the college entrance examination, plan ahead, and go from seeing flowers in the fog to seeing clearly as if watching a fire, so that you can have a million elite soldiers in your chest, fight on the battlefield, and defeat the enemy with ease. The guidance of famous teachers can turn iron into gold; a journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; a nine-story platform starts with a pile of soil, helping you take the first step in the college entrance examination review successfully!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate oneself is like having a golden key to happiness. Appreciating oneself does not mean being self-absorbed, it does not mean being self-centered, it does not mean being self-indulgent, and it certainly does not mean being narrow-minded... Give yourself some confidence, give yourself some joy, give yourself a smile, and who can worry about the lack of happiness in life? Celebrate for yourself often, and learn to find joy in your own company."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are gradually realizing that the Internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies, but rather inseparable \"twins.\" The retail industry is gradually showing signs of channel integration, with increasing online-offline penetration and convergence. Currently, Taobao has opened offline stores, and traditional companies are also increasingly venturing into the Internet. From GOME and Suning Appliance to Walmart and Carrefour, the list goes on."}
{"trans": "In summary, the commodity market is fraught with uncertainty, financial hegemony continues to manipulate the market, and the rules of the game change rapidly. Against the backdrop of a global debt crisis and mixed signals regarding the recovery of the world economy, the US dollar remains the most significant factor influencing the trend of bulk commodities. The economic policies of the US and Europe are closely intertwined, while domestic regulation adds to the mix. The interplay between the capital and confidence aspects, driven by these three factors, will inevitably lead to significant fluctuations in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "China Red is a thought-provoking spiritual culture, a unique spirit of the Chinese people, a powerful force of perseverance, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and unyielding determination, and a Chinese quality that has been passed down for thousands of years. The leading furniture company, Lian Tian Hong, has been spreading the fire of China Red with full passion, adhering to the business philosophy of integrity-based, and taking the lead in implementing workshop production transparency, setting an example for the industry, and rejuvenating the furniture industry."}
{"trans": "Character traits: In the Journey to the West, Tang Sanzang is tall, well-mannered, kind-hearted, and has a deep understanding of Buddhism. He encounters ninety-nine and eighty-one hardships on his journey to obtain the scriptures in the west, but remains steadfast in his pursuit. With the help of his disciples, Sun Wukong and Zhu Bajie, and the monk Sha, he overcomes countless hardships and finally obtains the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, whose dharma name is the行者 (行者, meaning \"the Walker\"), is Tang Sanzang's eldest disciple. He has a pair of fire-eyes that can see through anything, can transform into seventy-two different forms, and can travel through the clouds and mist. He detests evil, is fearless in the face of danger, is persistent, and is brave and courageous."}
{"trans": "Third, regarding studying: I have my own set of experiences— \"cultivating a sense of the question\" and \"getting less sleep.\" In fact, if you study until you become proficient, although you may not be able to solve problems immediately, you will have a better understanding of them. I do not advocate the \"flood of questions\" tactic, because we do not need to repeatedly solve the same or similar questions. Instead, we should compare and reflect on similar questions, and summarize the methods for solving them. The so-called \"sense of the question\" is similar to the \"language sense\" we often mention in English."}
{"trans": "The Great Wall of China, the longest man-made structure in the world, stretches over 6,700 kilometers across the rugged mountains in northern China. Its construction began during the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods. It is a rare ancient military defense engineering marvel in human architectural history, renowned for its long history, massive scale, and magnificent design. It has been listed as a World Heritage Site by UNESCO and is hailed as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "Because of the capital, they keep a low profile; because they are outstanding and cannot be vulgar, they keep a low profile. Essentially, luxury goods are outstanding, even unique. They absolutely cannot compromise on quality and fashion. They also have impeccable superiority in terms of art culture and style culture. Luxury goods are definitely not necessities in life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and profound brand heritage definitely make them necessary in life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt like they were filled with lead, she still strode across the street towards the parking garage. Now, she was drowsy and driving alone on the fluorescent concrete driveway, feeling dizzy. Seventeen hours ago, when she had just parked her car here, there were two station wagons parked on both sides, so close that she had to crawl out of the car. Now, her old \"Taurus\" car was like an orphan, standing alone in the eighth-floor parking area."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one knew that the Internet could move with a laptop, just as people could not imagine twenty years ago that a telephone could fit in a pocket and be with modern people's work and life at all times. Today, all kinds of smart terminals are exuding unprecedented magic, subtly changing human lifestyles. In the next decade, more subversive innovations are likely to emerge in the fields of terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics!"}
{"trans": "We advocate teamwork and we also admire the heroism of risking one's life to save comrades, but we must ensure that we do not become a burden to our comrades. We should try to avoid putting our comrades at unnecessary risk when rescuing us. Rigorous training and quick decision-making in the field are absolutely necessary! Before you have experienced the gunfire and bullets, don't play your paper-pushing tricks in front of us. Some things are not something that a young officer who has just come out of school can understand!"}
{"trans": "I blame myself for not deeply understanding the five-character poem of the poplar tree and my grandfather's seven-character poem. Although I have made progress in the art of \"pretending to be confused\" over time, I have not achieved a profound understanding. Last night, a mute mosquito bit my neck, and I shouted loudly, \"How can you bite people without making a sound? How can you suck blood without being honest? How can you not learn to be a decent mosquito, roaring towards my neck?\" Therefore, I live a tiring and absurd life, often hearing the humming laughter of mosquitoes and insects."}
{"trans": "When barbecues began to appear in every corner of the city like mushrooms after rain, people's nights became more and more flavorful, but it was really difficult to enjoy delicious food while also enjoying an elegant environment. When the sun set, the red sky met the lush green grass of the field, and under such a beautiful scenery, the tables were placed in a staggered manner according to the terrain, the barbecue masters skillfully grilled, the waiters swam back and forth, and the customers chatted happily, all feeling comfortable. The soothing music sounded in the ears, full of flavor."}
{"trans": "When I said this, the old man sighed deeply: \"Well, I have lived through nine deaths, it is truly indescribable!\" And so, this old man, who was proud and stubborn by nature, finally opened up to me, a writer he had never met before, about his bumpy life and inner world for the first time... In his narration, which was sometimes impassioned, sometimes heavy, sometimes filled with tears, and sometimes filled with laughter, I felt the tumultuous and tragic life of a 70-year-old man who had gone through many vicissitudes, as well as the irresistible manipulation of fate..."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, Western politics is far from as clean as people imagine. Beneath the facade of integrity and cleanliness, there is a flow of mud and murky water, albeit with a uniquely Western flavor. The politicians on stage \"sow\" with great dignity, while those below \"harvest\" in a reasonable and lawful manner. The cunning politicians and shrewd capitalists cooperate tacitly and understand each other without words. The tricks of officials and businessmen exchanging favors and trading power for money are played to a high degree of sophistication, to the point of being open and legal, to the point where Western democracy and the rule of law are powerless to stop them."}
{"trans": "After wading for several hours, a vast and open cave appeared before their eyes. “Oh my God, this isn’t an underground cave, it’s an underground forest!” the team members exclaimed. The cave was as large as a basketball court, with rugged rocks, flowing water, and deep ravines on the ground. Stalagmites as thick as a bowl were over 10 meters high, and there were huge curtains, uneven stalactites, and intricate pillars... all kinds of strange formations, just like a primeval forest. Moreover, the numerous crystals shone brightly under the light, making people feel as if they had entered a fairy tale world."}
{"trans": "The size of the heart can also be very small, only able to accommodate a home, a person, a sesame seed, or a drop of virus. A drizzle can drown it, a gust of wind can shatter it, a rumor can make it in unbearable pain, and a conspiracy can destroy it forever. The heart can be very hard, harder than any metal known to mankind. The heart can be very soft, weeping like silk or like a piece of cloth. The heart can be very resilient, enduring countless injuries and grievances, still as smooth as new. The heart can be very fragile, a moment of carelessness, and it can be instantly shattered."}
{"trans": "Walking through it, you can see the shady trees, the blooming flowers, the serene and tranquil beauty that is breathtaking; the gentle breeze, the pleasant fragrance, and suddenly you feel relaxed and refreshed. The winding stone paths, the well-arranged and sparse flowers and trees, the crisp and pleasant sound of the flowing water, the multi-layered scenery intertwined, forming a vivid and fragrant living picture. Every step changes the scenery, every flower and leaf, every grass and tree, every stone and spring, all exuding a unique charm, making you away from the hustle and bustle, feel the beauty of harmony between man and nature, and cleanse your soul. Enjoy the beauty here and enjoy the pleasure of life."}
{"trans": "The exasperated former whaling ship said, \"This is the whale we caught.\" The smug current whaling ship said, \"How did it end up here?\" The exasperated party said, \"It escaped again.\" The smug party said, \"Why didn't you tie it down properly?\" The exasperated party said:"}
{"trans": "Your sanctimonious appearance cannot hide your arrogance and greed! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, and slick con artists are mocking our incompetence—beware of slaps! You ungrateful husbands, who think you are so clever and capable, despise love and kindness."}
{"trans": "The two-month long farce has come to an end. We are not sure why Foxconn is so angry about these two reports. A wealthy company has no shortage of think tanks, and in addition to tearful apologies, there are also high-profile displays of anger as a crisis public relations tactic: perhaps to set an example, or perhaps to divert attention."}
{"trans": "Rewards should be given based on merit. This delicacy truly deserves it. \"I find you both pitiful and ridiculous, so arrogant,\" the wild duck replied. \"Your perspective is flawed. We wild ducks fly across the world, unattached and making the world our home. You, however, are dependent on others; we are self-sufficient, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the most difficult to write. It must be abrupt and vigorous, straightforward and to the point, and incisive in order to captivate the reader. There is no need to beat around the bush or use clichés. He also told me that when explaining something difficult to understand, using a metaphor can resolve all tangled arguments effortlessly. What an economical and skillful approach! This kind of thinking is very valuable."}
{"trans": "She began to read the fortune seriously. After a moment of busyness, she pretended to examine the sand table, calculated once, then looked up at Kudi and said, \"You damn shameless fellow! You dare to talk nonsense in front of me! The fortune clearly states that you are Kudi, a bandit who commits murder, theft, and every other evil act, and is beyond redemption.\""}
{"trans": "The castle truly was like a paradise. As he gazed at the magnificent building, he was filled with wonder, awe, and envy. They strolled through the gardens, picked fresh fruit to eat, and were completely enchanted by the atmosphere filled with birdsong and flowers. They lingered there for so long that they lost track of time. When they had finally finished touring the entire castle, it was already dark, and they returned to the hall by the pool, planning to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning really works well. The cool and fresh air, the well-organized layout, the well-dressed guests, and the courteous staff all make this place feel like a hidden paradise, exceptionally comfortable. It's always the people who ruin the atmosphere. Those well-dressed gentlemen were all eating with greasy faces, which was very uncomfortable to watch. They all nodded to Nikolai, and for some reason, some of them even gave him a meaningful look."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to falter, and as they saw that their situation was desperate, they finally abandoned their resistance and fled to the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth, sweeping away the remaining enemy. They were like two majestic land dragons, advancing with unstoppable force, crushing everything in their path, reducing the enemy's fortified positions to rubble, and sending the slower enemies to their doom. They were a poignant declaration of victory by the Chinese army, heralding the imminent demise of the stubborn invaders."}
{"trans": "After this disaster, our family never recovered. Our fortune declined, and we fell into poverty, struggling to survive in hunger and cold. The old locust tree lost its former glory, and the remaining half of the tree stump stood alone and forlorn in the half-barren courtyard, enduring wind, rain, dew, and frost for many years. It neither sprouted buds nor grew branches, and no one paid attention to it. It could only stand there upright and sigh to the sky."}
{"trans": "Anything reactionary will not fall unless you strike it. Dust will not disappear on its own without a broom. You are all finished, but I, Zhang Puxing, a loyal Bolshevik, am upright, clean, sincere, and devoted. The revolution is not a dinner party, not an article, not a painting or embroidery, not frying oil sticks. The proletariat has suppressed all of you demons."}
{"trans": "Overly idolizing top-performing students in the college entrance examination can make them feel superior. Some develop a sense of complacency, arrogance, and self-importance, and unconsciously lower their standards in their future work and life, becoming self-centered and finding it difficult to cooperate with others. Others may believe that they must always be better than others, excessively pursuing perfection, being overly cautious, and following rules strictly. These attitudes may make former top-performing students lack creativity and passion, ultimately hindering their success."}
{"trans": "I will treat every patient equally, regardless of whether their clothes are luxurious or tattered, whether their appearance is handsome or ugly, whether they are wealthy or impoverished, whether their status is high or low, whether they are spotless or riddled with wounds, whether they have complex or minor ailments, whether they are polite or rude to me, whether they are cultured or illiterate, whether they are humorous or dull, whether they are high-ranking officials or ordinary citizens..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That spontaneous admiration, that uncontrollable longing, that deep affection shared through thick and thin, that sincere love that sustains each other through hardships—these are the deepest comfort and the most solid support in life. And all of this is free. It cannot be bought with money. Having a goal is free. Whether you are a prince with fine clothes and rich food or a beggar with tattered clothes, as long as you are willing, you can set a goal for your life. This goal can be great or ordinary, brilliant or simple. As long as you are willing, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should focus your energy on planning the path to success, and then move forward with all your might. During this period, you must not be distracted, look left and right, or change your mind at the sight of something different. In this process, you should strictly eliminate doubts and fears, because they will undermine your determination, disrupt your motivation, and affect your actions to achieve your goals with all your might. Those who are filled with doubts and fears will ultimately achieve nothing and have nothing. When doubts and fears infiltrate your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all strong thoughts will be severely impacted and collapse."}
{"trans": "A cultured person has a deep respect and admiration for the noble qualities of humanity, such as loyalty, courage, trust, diligence, mutual assistance, self-sacrifice, fearlessness, perseverance, and steadfastness. Not everyone may be able to put these qualities into practice, but they understand how to cherish and praise them. A person may not be free from cowardice and laziness, but he cannot disguise these vices as high moral standards, nor can he, because he cannot achieve nobility, denigrate all those who have achieved these qualities as hypocrites. You can kneel in the mud, but you cannot smear mud all over the world's chest and then solemnly declare that everywhere is filthy."}
{"trans": "In this world, there are quiet beginnings, explosive beginnings, cautious beginnings, bold beginnings, secretive beginnings, half-hearted beginnings, sinister beginnings, and honest beginnings. Different people give their lives different ways to begin. These ways reflect a person's mindset, vision, courage, stature, and integrity in managing their life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the final stage of review plays a crucial role in the entire preparation process. Therefore, we should pay great attention to the final stage of review and avoid making mistakes that could lead to wasted efforts and missed opportunities for success. Below, we will explain several common misconceptions."}
{"trans": "The market is currently leaderless, with major sectors taking turns to adjust, with weak support, making it very difficult for mainstream capital to operate, so the market is very weak, like a frightened bird, and panics at the slightest negative news, leading to increased panic selling, while off-exchange capital continues to wait and see, and with the holiday season approaching, there is little desire to go long, making the market even more lackluster."}
{"trans": "The stubborn Japanese, who were already struggling to survive, had a battle line that was as fragile as a ship with a thousand holes leaking water from all sides. This fatal blow immediately shattered their defenses like weathered rock. In fact, stopping the armored train was not difficult; all that was needed was to dismantle the tracks beforehand."}
{"trans": "Distinguishing between genuine and fake: How to tell the difference? More and more people are becoming aware of and fond of walnut collectibles, and market prices are rising. There are also many cases of forgeries using high-tech methods. Lao Hu was initially fooled, but now he has seen enough to be wise. He now sleeps with walnuts in his hand, and is no longer easily fooled. He shared several methods for distinguishing between genuine and fake with the readers of the evening newspaper."}
{"trans": "In my life, I have walked and crossed the broad avenues and small wooden bridges, just like everyone else. I have faced many ups and downs, twists and turns, and have come this far. I cannot deny that I have been fortunate, and the success and hollow fame I have achieved are somewhat undeserved. On the other hand, I have also experienced misfortunes that are rare for others. During that infamous so-called \"Great Revolution,\" I almost lost my life for daring to speak out for justice. The physical suffering is also unforgettable."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang is arguably one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. He compared himself to Guan Zhong in Longzhong, demonstrating an incredible level of confidence! His prediction of dividing the country into three was remarkably accurate! When he first emerged from obscurity, he faced Xiahou Dun's 100,000-strong army without fear; the burning of Bomo Slope impressed Guan Yu and Zhang Fei; the burning of Xinye left Cao Ren heartbroken; his clever schemes, such as tricking Zhou Yu three times, were not only brilliant but also humorous; despite being loyal to Liu Bei, he refused to be crowned emperor; his calm demeanor when implementing the Empty City Strategy due to a misjudgment in decision-making is truly admirable. However, what moved me the most was not these, but \"The Autumn Wind at Wuzhang Plain\"."}
{"trans": "As night falls in the mountain village, we hear a series of sharp dog barks. After midnight, the barking becomes intermittent, and the lights in the windows begin to flicker on and off, like cabbage leaves with their pure white faces... The moonlight washes over the water pipes in the courtyard..."}
{"trans": "A shot from close range went wide; a header in front of the goal went astray; even a one-on-one opportunity was missed... The national youth team's ability to seize opportunities is disappointing, especially since they lack opportunities to train in domestic leagues. This is currently the biggest weakness of this national youth team."}
{"trans": "However, in a sociological sense, the current Israeli and Palestinian sides are irreconcilable enemies. This is due to the estrangement, indifference, suspicion, and hostility caused by the fact that the two brothers were separated for over 1,000 years after the Jewish people fled Palestine in 556 BC and scattered around the world, as well as the return of the Jewish people to Palestine and the establishment of the State of Israel two millennia later. As a result, the mutual conflict has turned into a massacre, and the fraternal relationship has been completely destroyed."}
{"trans": "National policies have come down from above, and the industry situation has taken a sharp turn for the worse. The ceramic production areas have been hit the hardest, like wild beasts trapped in a predicament. The production areas are struggling, and the ceramic enterprises are searching for a way forward. The cold wave has brought not only shocks and pain to the production areas, but also made them see the future path more clearly. Read more: The industry situation has taken a sharp turn for the worse, and many ceramic production areas are struggling like trapped beasts."}
{"trans": "Stepping into Suyuan, walking through the Suzhou courtyard, you can see small bridges and flowing water, white walls and black tiles, or winding paths leading to secluded places, or peaks and turns. The most profound feeling is that the rigorous and meticulous construction process of the garden is similar to that of the imperial gardens in the Forbidden City. The layout of corridors, pavilions, and water pavilions is layered and staggered; walking on a 20-meter path gives a feeling of openness over 3-5 li, and suddenly feels like walking in a painting."}
{"trans": "The battlefield situation is ever-changing, and there is no set formula for winning battles since ancient times. How to deploy troops, attack or defend, engage in positional warfare or maneuver warfare, voluntarily abandon or hold onto a city, which part to abandon and which part to hold, etc., all should be decided by the frontline commanders themselves, and the commander-in-chief should not interfere too much. In fact, any strategic tactics can be integrated and applied flexibly, and it is not possible to say which battle method is necessarily superior. This is the \"many roads lead to Rome\", and winning battles is the only hard truth."}
{"trans": "A novel is a backlight of the soul. You inject a part of your soul into your work, giving it your flesh and blood, and thus achieving artistic greatness. This involves two issues: first, writers need to examine their true state of soul and first shape themselves; second, the power of sincerity is immense, and the significance of sincerity here is not only to correct excessive deviations, but also to abandon the trend of contrived, servile, sensational, and opportunistic creation. Do not scratch the itch with a pole, do not fart in public, and do not sell sincerity like a dog-skin plaster. I believe sincerity should be an attitude of survival, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The old locust tree outside the window, weathered by wind and frost, and the moon hanging motionless on the motionless branches like a bell, yet so far from the sound of the bell. I know that if there is dust, don't expect it to make a golden sound when it falls to the ground. Yet it is this dust-like moonlight that makes the silent midnight feel more like a midnight shipwreck."}
{"trans": "Ruthless and cold-hearted, cunning and treacherous, yet I am kind-hearted and generous, and I seek to save all beings. In the gloomy House of Death, I am engrossed in drawing talismans and writing incantations when suddenly I hear the anguished voice of Toboso's Dulcinea, and I learn that she has unfortunately been ensnared by magic."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dan Dan, who suspects Alibaba of having a \"cross the river and demolish the bridge\" mentality, believes that \"capital has its own nature, and it is only natural for them to consider the interests of their shareholders. Taking over an investment means taking over the capital contract. One cannot worship it like a god when it is needed, and demonize it when it is an obstacle.\""}
{"trans": "Even the sharpest eyes are powerless! The sight is overwhelming, and one dares not look directly at the throne. We come from the East, and the trouble is in the West; the line is long and stretches far—from the front to the back, one cannot see the end. They press forward, one after another, their courage growing, spears in hand, ten against one, a hundred against ten, and thousands of lives disappear without a trace."}
{"trans": "Just as he was feeling elated after acquiring the emerald green jade, he went on a long trip. When he returned home, he learned from his family members that the emerald green jade and a bag of gold and silver from home had disappeared. Upon hearing this news, he was furious, bristling with anger, beating and scolding himself, and even tearing his clothes. The thought of his efforts coming to naught made him even more angry."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. In the field of corporate public relations and marketing in China, it was a year of turmoil and strife. For corporate marketing and public relations personnel, it seemed that \"public relations crises\" suddenly appeared like ferocious beasts, causing fear and anxiety. Time flew by quickly, and soon we would enter 2009. Looking back on this year, many business owners are still haunted by their experiences, walking on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leo friends are almost always willing to take on new work tasks, as long as they can showcase their talents and abilities. They will grit their teeth and help out, but this naturally leads to them easily forgetting things and accumulating a significant amount of work. Therefore, a handy calendar and weekly schedule are the most appropriate office good-luck items for them. Especially those with a lively and playful style, which perfectly matches their pure-hearted nature, allowing them to handle tasks with ease even when they are very busy."}
{"trans": "A good essay should contain six or seven excellent sentences: one is a vivid and beautiful metaphorical sentence; two is a grand and parallel sentence; three is an emotional personification sentence; four is a profound and paraphrased sentence; five is a philosophical sentence that inspires the mind; six is a contrasting sentence that complements the whole; seven is a poetic and beautiful sentence. By skillfully using these excellent sentences, the essay will be concise, profound, and vivid, with a dragon's eye, shining throughout the whole, and the literary talent will naturally increase."}
{"trans": "What is even more ridiculous is that Western countries' economies are still stagnant, their printing presses are running at full capacity, and their treasuries are empty, yet they still expect China to \"feed\" the world... Now everyone is turning their attention to China, the world's second largest economy. If the post-Cold War global system controlled by the United States is on the verge of collapse, will this emerging economic superpower step forward? Or will it let the West reap what it has sown? But this time, China may be unwilling and unable to help!"}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for 54 years, expanding the territory of China to form a vast domain stretching from Liaodong and Korea in the east to the present-day Balkhash Lake in the west, from the central region of Vietnam in the south to the Khingan Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north. The population under his rule reached nearly 60 million. To be fair, among the hundreds of emperors in Chinese history, very few could expand the territory like Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che. The others were lucky if they could preserve their family business and not become prodigal sons who brought shame and loss to their country. From this perspective alone, Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, should be regarded as a truly capable and far-sighted emperor."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivial matters of ordinary people's lives, lacking twists and turns, but they are refreshing due to their unique perspective and undeniable personal bias. He is adept at creating one-of-a-kind, personalized characters, which is precisely the hallmark of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people make a show of bravado, flaunting their credentials and industry leadership, seeking selling points and packaging themselves, endlessly promoting and selling themselves amidst the flood of information. Others, with a mindset of keeping their wealth hidden, or focusing solely on their own self-improvement, quietly work hard and avoid drawing attention to themselves."}
{"trans": "In fact, why do \"verbal battles\" always seem to be overwhelming and persist for months? What forces are behind this? What exactly is subtly influencing netizens' judgments and thoughts? Not only ordinary netizens, but even some website administrators are puzzled by this."}
{"trans": "That evening, he spread out his writing paper and prepared to write an article to earn back the 20 yuan. That night, the title of his article was: On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality. He said: In this era of fallen materialism, we must hold high the banner of morality to oppose materialism. That night, his paper was vigorous, passionate, and heartfelt, filled with righteous indignation, and flowed like a river, sweeping away all obstacles."}
{"trans": "1. The application essay should have a far-sighted perspective. As an official essay, the most basic characteristic of an application essay is that its intention and theme should be lofty. The essay should focus on long-term benefits, see the essence through phenomena, be good at giving high-level guidance, and be good at sublimating the theme. In other words, the essay should have a lofty ideological realm, and must not be vulgar, much less low-class, or full of complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a manifestation of compassion for those who suffer. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of those who seek the unknown, like stardust in a child's eyes, or a piece of bread in one's throat."}
{"trans": "Look up again, and see how slender her shoulders are! They are like twin lambs, or like two jade peaks; they are as lean as autumn mountains and as flat as autumn waters. Above the shoulders, you see the face that people usually sing praises for."}
{"trans": "Even lotus flowers have their own tragic stories of clan annihilation. The lotus petals, with their thousand fingers, hold onto a summer and then let go of another. Now it is the ghostly rain of autumn night, falling noisily onto the surface of the water, like a disheveled and blind-eyed Chopin abusing a thousand-key piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moon adds depth to one's purpose; discussing swordsmanship under the moon makes one's liver and gallbladder more genuine; discussing poetry under the moon adds elegance to one's style; and facing a beautiful woman under the moon deepens one's affection. The way to enjoy the moon: when it is bright, it is best to look up; when it is hazy, it is best to look down. Spring wind is like wine; summer wind is like tea; autumn wind is like smoke; winter wind is like mustard."}
{"trans": "He arrived in this damp and cold world, riding the waves of blood in a small red boat. His final leap was propelled through the gates of life by a torrent of heat, like the mud and debris swept away by a flood. The excited cries of the babies echoed like glass cups shattering against each other."}
{"trans": "If China has one more gloomy writer, this north-facing study room should be held responsible. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit full of southern flavors that has been refrigerated. During the day, I seem to be immersed in the depths of the ocean, where the quiet darkness plays a gray melody."}
{"trans": "The red candle has a spirit; it does not cherish its life, yet it is particularly attached to it. Every time it is about to burn out, the charred wick raises and convulses high in the flame, as if the spine of a warrior suddenly shot in mid-air, becoming an unyielding sculpture, then sinks heavily into the fiery blood pool..."}
{"trans": "When you go outside and look up at the sky, you can see the grid-like structure of the heavens, and the morning dew falls after the rain, and the sun rises, with silver beads scattered all over, shining brightly, creating countless suns from a single one. There is no need to sweep away the old net in the corner of the wall; let the dust settle, and over time, the rope will become thicker, like the roots of an old tree, and can be used as a three-dimensional mural, reading tradition and modernity, always new and fresh."}
{"trans": "Spring is always the first to knock on the bamboo gate of the garden, and then, it lights up the extinguished torches from last year, one by one. At this time, winter, which has been alone in the empty house, is like a howling wolf that flees in the sudden flames. The flames make its lonely gaze bewildered, and the flower skirt of the earth makes it lost."}
{"trans": "The methods used to punish evil are more evil than the evil itself, and the indiscriminate killing of innocent people is as easy as cutting grass. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, and righteousness, there is a sea of swords and bloodshed, and the cost of this grand ambition is a landscape littered with corpses. The basic value of life is reduced to a few withered blades of grass under the hooves of horses; the right to survival of the common people is as fleeting as a few bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "—The heavenly sound, the infinite mystery, the infinite encirclement of the finite, or the stern yet gentle command of God. Music is the omniscient and omnipotent God of notes, who is both the creator—arranging and defining the positions of the notes—and the savior—if the notes can listen and follow the ceaseless and unremitting playing."}
{"trans": "On the winding lotus pond, the water lilies spread out like a sea of leaves. The leaves rise high above the water, like the skirts of graceful dancers. Among the layers of leaves, white flowers are scattered here and there, some blooming gracefully, others shyly closed; they resemble pearls, stars in the blue sky, or beautiful women who have just bathed."}
{"trans": "Therefore, when it comes to cities, if everything you see and encounter is young and vibrant, it must be that the time is not yet right, and the strings of the lute are not yet in tune. This is like writing; when adjectives are used like a girl in full makeup, and parallel sentences like lovers walking side by side, it is certain that the way of writing has not yet been mastered. The ultimate expression in writing is like an old street with sparse willows, old seats under the willows, and casual conversations between seats, with a delicate and relaxed style."}
{"trans": "The suffering of individual families does not affect the happiness of the world. Summer arrives irresistibly, and the kapok flowers, like pink butterflies, flutter around the lonely and desolate hospital windowsill. The girl's head has become a polygon, and the healed bone seams, like cracked land, stretch out black holes beneath the thin skin, with an inner demon expanding in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit full of southern flavors that has been refrigerated in a freezer. During the day, I seem to be immersed in the silence of the ocean floor, where the gray music of the deep darkness plays. At night, I seem to hear the sound of an Eskimo's sled sliding, and the long beard of the North Star hangs down, ringing the strings of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the moon, not wanting to disturb anyone, yet they have truly disturbed a large area, which can truly be described as \"the moon's appearance startles the mountain birds\". Compared to Tao Yuanming's quietness, Wang Wei's quietness has a bit of a noble air and a bit of exquisite design. His brilliance lies in being more like a commoner than a noble and designing more naturally than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even the brown coffee table was painted with emotion, a gentle rectangle that bore the weight of all the lively activity on it. There was also a larger one, with white magnolias, thin and shiny, resembling both crystal and the coolness of a jade fish that Yang Gui would hold in his mouth when his milk teeth hurt. The resilient lines of the forsythia opened and closed with determination, its control over life was both composed and domineering."}
{"trans": "\"Vast and desolate, I shall return to the great wilderness!\" When I read this passage, I didn't feel sad, but rather beautiful. It was like reading the \"Records of the Grand Historian\" and coming across the scene where Jing Ke, dressed in white, crossed the Yi River to assassinate the King of Qin. The passage was full of color. Imagine a young master from a wealthy family, having seen through the world, standing in the snow with a red cape, barefoot and with a shaved head, bidding farewell to his father. How beautiful that would be!"}
{"trans": "We cannot transcend that dark, humiliating, and indifferent Chengde era, just as we cannot avoid facing the ugly and desolate Taoist tower when approaching the Mogao Caves. No matter how splendid and magnificent our memories of Dunhuang may be, they ultimately cannot fill the vast scripture cave, cannot wash away the pale whiteness in the Thousand Buddha Grottoes, nor can they soothe the blood-stained wounds of the ancient ethnic group on the horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetting visits us more and more frequently and becomes a lifelong friend. I use this friend to filter out what is unnecessary to remember. The subconscious controls memory, just as the wind directs a kite on an invisible level. New, powerful threads weave an uneven sieve of memory, and the remaining lumps are like cheese, sweet and containing hard, tooth-breaking pieces."}
{"trans": "His chest was broad and upright, containing the earth-shattering roar of his ancestors when they chased wild beasts. His pelvis was deeply indented, and the sharp, protruding bones indicated that powerful muscle groups had once attached there, pulling the entire body through lizard-like climbing, like the ropes of the Yellow River boatmen. His limbs were like the long, beautiful ivory of African elephants, emitting a smooth, lustrous shine like melted fat."}
{"trans": "It wasn't until years later that I let go of my resentment and admitted that day was a perilous curve in my life. What caused me to abandon the withered roses was not the art teacher's sarcasm, but the sight of your dazzling talent, which made me break my brush with a gesture of regret. What is regret like? It's like a tiny mole on your body, only you know its location and the process of its appearance."}
{"trans": "I combed my hair on the balcony, and my hair fell like autumn leaves, coming down in clumps, fluttering down my arm like a night rain. Far and near, many car horns were sounding off in a panic; the sky, gradually darkening, spread out like a vast lake of smoke and mist. Across the way, a faint wisp of cooking smoke emerged from a window on the lowest level of a building, rising very hesitantly, as if unsure of where the sky was."}
{"trans": "She was carrying two water jugs in each hand, which reminded me of a woman walking gracefully on a thin rope. This was all because of her waist; her waist was so soft that, to put it in simple terms, it was soft enough to make me feel like I was eating Suzhou nougat. Not only her waist, but as my diary says: she had a set of curves that rivaled the beauty of the clouds and the moon, woven into a large, seductive net!"}
{"trans": "Because of your language, your silence, when you sink to the deepest point, you let yourself disappear. Losing your language, and thus losing yourself, losing your existence, Yang Lian thus realized that he had become a \"ghost\"; a ghost floating between cities, watching coldly (like an insect, a ghost is also an \"it\", can only watch), watching the complete annihilation of \"meaning\". There is a sea, but the port is meaningless to you."}
{"trans": "A lamp is far away from another, and there is darkness between the bright and bright. My shadow sometimes appears in the bright and sometimes disappears in the dark. The wind that comes out of nowhere stirs the colorful fallen leaves wave after wave, just like it stirs the impressions of life. I feel like I am this empty wind, and I can only capture my own existence when I shed and swirl the colorful fallen leaves."}
{"trans": "But we, standing on the open land—my father, my brother, my relatives, and many villagers who have shed blood, sweat under the sun, and braved rain and wind—stood there, listening to the distant thunder, and no one seemed to want to go inside to escape the northwest rain. Our hearts were heavier than the dry sky, and we all remained silent, because our hearts were also filled with rain, and this heart-rain seemed even more tragic and relentless than the northwest rain."}
{"trans": "Imagine if Tang Bohu and Emperor Qianlong were both considered \"first-rate poets of ancient China.\" In that case, we would have no choice but to quietly burn the entire \"Complete Tang Poems\" collection. The same goes for calligraphy. An astonishingly high price paid for a mediocre brush and ink is like a pile of gold tipping the scales of Chinese calligraphy history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the literary tradition is hidden, a small hill is considered a peak; when the strong wings are far away, broken feathers are considered a peng.\""}
{"trans": "The attack came suddenly, as if the girl had received a command from the heavens, and she convulsed without any warning. The soft girl shrank like a hard whipping stick, and every muscle shone like iron. Her small body arched like a drawn bow, bouncing on the pale, snow-white bed, and countless drops of sweat dripped from this grotesque human rainbow bridge, like snow melting from the eaves in spring."}
{"trans": "This unleashed power is lonely yet powerful, both conventional and unconventional, intoxicated yet poetic, akin to the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu wielded his brush like a staggering drunk, swaying, dancing with his hands and feet, his posture graceful and energetic, completing all movements in one go, then throwing down his cup and laughing, falling into a deep sleep. Zhang Xu did not know that his staggering steps were also the footsteps of Tang culture."}
{"trans": "But when I held my breath and listened intently, we all suddenly and simultaneously stopped talking. This cicada scared me again! Like a rope, the cicada's sound tied my heart tightly, and then it suddenly loosened without any warning, so my heart scattered without preparation, like waves struggling to leap into the sky and accidentally falling onto the beach! I don't even know when summer crossed the threshold!"}
{"trans": "I have wept for your humiliation and disappointment. My tears flowed like streams, clear as crystal, but they could not wash away the thick dirt on you, only the veil from my eyes. These tears could not moisten your stony hearts, only extinguish the flames of anxiety and longing in my heart. Now, faced with your suffering, I laugh, a laugh that thunders, not after the storm, but before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually understood that in the face of disaster, one cannot use the grammar of disaster; there is another grammar that leads directly to the poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From then on, my state of life was no longer the same; every time I read Zhuangzi's chapters such as \"Autumn Water,\" \"逍遥游,\" \"齐物论,\" and \"天下,\" it was like looking at electrocardiograms that were relevant to me. It is difficult for me to make a calm and impartial assessment of such a philosopher who is too close to me, so I can only avoid it."}
{"trans": "You pressed your forehead against the embroidered flowers on the fabric. When the sun was on this side, it would bake the gold thread until it was scorching hot, but now it has grown cold. The people who lived here in the past had lived a hard life, and their deeds and actions had gradually become covered in dust. When their descendants hung their clothes to dry, the dust would be shaken off and would dance in the yellow sunlight. If memories had a scent, it would be the scent of camphor, sweet and steady, like a clearly remembered happiness, sweet and poignant, like a forgotten sorrow."}
{"trans": "It is this state of affairs that allows them to be close to life, and enables us to be close to them even a thousand years later. Yang Guifei's liveliness, I think, is like a ceramic soup pot, smooth and jade-like, at your feet, and when the water inside gradually cools down, it gives a gentle, stubborn feeling. Su Qing, however, is a small red clay stove with its own independent fire. You can see the red flames and hear the sound of chestnuts exploding when they are peeled, but it is more difficult to take care of, as you need to add coal and wood, and the smoke is irritating."}
{"trans": "Like a surging wave, the sound of the cicadas beats against the emotions that have settled in your heart. In an instant, you feel that the sound of the cicadas, like the raging waves washing away the sand, has taken away the light sorrow that you were holding on to. The abrupt cessation of the urgent sound of the cicadas at the highest note is more like a beautiful article being suddenly torn apart, with the sonorous words scattered on the ground, resounding like the sound of gold and stone, and then becoming a fragmented and incomplete piece, leaving only some melancholy and some nostalgia for people to ponder. Is it not also a song of life?"}
{"trans": "There are active youths here, there are hot and passionate hearts, there are no decadent old people, only strong young seniors. The silver-white moon wanders aimlessly in the empty sky, as if it is shedding tears, hating its loneliness. … And there is that swimming pool, always smiling like a kind old lady with wrinkles all over her face. When she sees many lively children jumping into the water like little mermaids, she is so happy that she bursts out a huge silver splash."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, the wasteland was lost to history. On one side of the wasteland were shadowy, unknown master craftsmen, and on the other side was a frightened contemporary woman. The kilns on both sides burned with fierce flames, like two beacon towers separated by thousands of miles, but the signals they transmitted were accurate. While many other beacon towers were associated with war, these two were not. Separated by the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, only two wisps of the purest, lightest smoke remained, echoing across the distance."}
{"trans": "Lin Daiyu's brokenness stems from her deep-seated love; Sanmao's brokenness comes from her sudden enlightenment and detachment after experiencing many vicissitudes; Van Gogh's brokenness is the continuous pain in the light caused by the golden knife of the sun; Beethoven's brokenness is the tragic symphony of life struck by the extreme spiritual black and white keys. If the brokenness of ordinary people reveals the purest and most beautiful light of humanity, then the brokenness of these excellent souls is like silver fireworks blooming in the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "No matter how many times you wash your face a day, it still won’t be clean. Your eyes never need washing, and they will always be bright. There’s no need to spend money on a mop and broom for the empty space, since people are mobile and naturally dust-repelling. Strangely, the air isn’t thin because of the small space. To see people’s breath, I used a cigarette as a visible representation of the air, inhaling once and exhaling three times, rising majestically to the ceiling. After admiring the abundance of the world below, I looked up and saw how vast the universe is."}
{"trans": "Knowing oneself without knowing others is merely a way of gathering in one corner and living out one's life without interacting with others; it is no more than a summer insect that cannot speak of ice, a frog at the bottom of a well, or a donkey in a mill. True self-awareness comes from knowing others; just like the princess Iron Fan's fan, it must be able to extend before it can retract. The more one knows, the broader one's understanding; by scattering oneself throughout the world and permeating into all things to observe their size, shape, weight, and density, one can gradually and accurately recognize one's true self."}
{"trans": "The singing is like flowing clouds and water, dispelling worries and allowing one to wander within it. It is like surging waves and terrifying tides, striking the emotions that have settled in your heart, and in an instant, you feel that the sound of the cicadas, like the waves washing away the sand, has taken away the light sorrow that you were holding on to tightly. The urgency of the cicada's sound suddenly stops at the highest note, more like a beautiful article being suddenly torn apart, with the sonorous words scattered on the ground, falling like the sound of gold and stone, and then becoming a simple and incomplete piece, leaving only some melancholy and some sentimentality for people to ponder."}
{"trans": "What is there to be nihilistic about? God's affairs are unknown to man; man's affairs are about constructing and connecting meaning in the midst of fate's constraints—or perhaps helplessly—thereby saving the present and also saving eternity. Therefore, the \"eternal return\" is by no means a \"total affirmation of earthly life,\" but merely means that man cannot escape earthly life, not even in death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence of eternity, that is, the earth's gaze towards the sky—that grand music has always filled heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "However, the experience of viewing Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings is completely different. It feels as if we are reading Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei's pastoral poems late at night. With just a few strokes and light ink, it does not stir up our hearts with intense emotions, but rather calms them down. It is not about filling our hearts with something, but rather washing away the mundane thoughts that fill our hearts, just like the mountain streams after a heavy rain. The water is initially turbid, but as the rain clears and the sky turns blue, the entire stream becomes clear, and the mud and dirt in the mountains are washed away."}
{"trans": "The sound was sometimes slow and sometimes fast, sometimes high and sometimes low, sometimes loud and sometimes soft, sometimes continuous and sometimes intermittent. At times it was like the sound of gold and jade resonating, at other times like the great bell of Huang Zhong, and sometimes like large pearls falling onto a jade plate. At times it was like red coral and white agate sinking into the sea, and sometimes like playing a plain silk zither. At times it was like dancing with thunder, at other times like a hundred birds singing in harmony, and sometimes like a rabbit falling and a hawk rising. My imagination ran wild, I couldn't control myself, my heart was in full bloom, and the wind was dancing at the tip of my pen. The dead characters seemed to come alive, and I felt full of youthful vitality once again. I have rarely reached such a spiritual state in my life, and it is even more difficult to explain to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps the clouds are meant to float in the sky, unlike the sun, which has fiery wheels for feet, so they will not descend to accept my warm hospitality. But perhaps this is just my delusion. However, this delusion is a bit too beautiful. If the blue sky is a book without words, the clouds must be the footnotes, and my rapid car tracks translating the language of the clouds on the road are the latest published commentaries. The sky is written in changing blue, the clouds are painted with clean hands, and then handed to my eyes to be printed. We are all telling the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "I couldn’t eat it on the plane, and when I returned to the United States and tried it, it was too greasy and too spicy, which was not like the sausage roll that I occasionally ate with my father. In Shanghai, right next to our house was the Qishilin Café, which had recently moved from Tianjin during the war. They baked bread every dawn, and the smell of the bread acted as an alarm, filling the air with a fragrant and powerful aroma that seemed to come from afar, and yet it was the gentlest of alarm clocks, never waking one up at the wrong time, and like the annoying spring colors, it was something one couldn’t help but be affected by. Having such a “fragrant” neighbor was truly a nuisance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like a sugar cube used to entice children to take medicine, or an electric rabbit used to lure dogs to race in a dog racing field. A few minutes or days of happiness make us endure a lifetime of suffering. We hope it comes, hope it stays, and hope it comes again—these three sentences sum up the entire history of human endeavor. While we pursue and wait, life slips by unnoticed. Perhaps we are merely pawns in the consumption of time, living a lifetime as sacrificial offerings for the years, without ever thinking of happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a dark green silk with large black shadows that seem to be filled with thunder and lightning. There is also a Japanese silk fabric in a light lake color that shimmers with wood and water patterns. Every few steps, two teacup-sized plum blossoms float on the water, with iron outlines and silver hooks, like the stained glass windows in a medieval chapel, with heavy iron borders embedded in red glass. The most common colors on the market are those that cannot be named, not quite blue, not quite gray, not quite yellow, and can only be used as backgrounds. These are neutral colors, also known as protective colors, civilized colors, or mixed colors."}
{"trans": "This is due to her movements; her every step, every stretch, every glance, every bow, even the slight movement of her sleeves and the gentle sway of her skirt, are like the flow of honey and the gentle ripple of the wind; how could we not be delighted and amazed? The most lovely thing is her soft waist; the ancients said that the willow tree bending in the wind, and in \"Dream of the Red Chamber\" it was said that Qingwen had a water snake waist, all of which refer to the slenderness of the waist; but the waist I love is simply like the cowhide candy from Suzhou, making my whole mouth sweet and my teeth soft. Her waist is so soft, and her hands and feet are also extraordinarily graceful."}
{"trans": "There were some wine bottles leaning crookedly beside me, with not much wine left. Unfortunately, I don’t drink alcohol, otherwise, at a time like this, taking a sip or two would be a wonderful pleasure. “Raising a cup to invite the moon,” the moon would shyly peek into your cup; a gentle breeze would pass by, and you could hear the rustling of the trees on the mountains on both sides, and the lights would appear and disappear, like naughty children playing hide-and-seek with you. Coupled with the shimmering scales on the river surface, it was like a symphony of a dreamlike scene. What kind of earthly dream is this?"}
{"trans": "I can no longer tell clearly, with the real sun shining on the stage, how could there be such a sense of desolation? There is a place where art and reality overlap, becoming blurred; it is like holding a matchstick in the sunlight, burning slowly and hazily, you can't see the faint orange-yellow flame very clearly, but you can more distinctly feel that your hand is also a temporary thing in the sunlight... The maid on stage sang for a while, holding a tea tray, and moved through the rooms in a sweeping gesture, crossing countless thresholds, and came to the study, bowing to the cousin and raising the tea tray to eye level."}
{"trans": "I saw a tabby cat lying lazily under a dilapidated wall, morning glories blooming in a riot of deep green and purple, and the cat stretching itself nonchalantly. In the hazy night, I saw the streetlights casting the shadows of the transformers on the sidewalk onto a white construction wall, with the swaying shadows of the trees intermingling with the real shadows, looking like the balcony where Romeo sang his love song to Juliet. I saw the face of the poet Zhou Mengdie, who, as I waved goodbye to him, happened to be framed in a small window of a moving bus, as if the entire bus, with utmost solemnity, was framing a picture for him."}
{"trans": "You think that the innocent heart, which is naked and loves everything, can be seen in the faint morning mist, and no matter how you beckon with your hand, it always doesn’t return to your throat; how “lacking” is that? So Pingbo felt suffocated, and then, like the soft breeze in spring whispering among the green trees, he quietly and intimately told you about his unforgettable “childhood”. Although he couldn’t stay in that “childhood” forever, if he could invite a few companions to wander around a few times, he could slightly reduce his feeling of emptiness, and the taste of melancholy wouldn’t always be stuck on his tongue."}
{"trans": "You could also say that it is the starting point for the Chinese people's journey towards modernity, but which nation's steps towards modernity have ever been as hurried, panicky, self-doubting, and chaotic as those in Shanghai? You could also say that it is a city civilization that has risen up in opposition to agricultural civilization, but which city civilization has ever been as constantly coveted, disintegrated, surrounded, and enveloped by the immense rural forces as Shanghai? In short, it is a huge paradox: when you look at its filth, it emits a dazzling light; when you worship its power, it turns around to show you its scarred back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the reality is quite the opposite. I sat there quietly, listening to the sound of raindrops above my head. At that moment, sound was better than silence, and I felt boundless joy in my heart, as if I had drunk fairy dew and inhaled essence, feeling as if I was floating in the air. The sound was sometimes slow and sometimes fast, sometimes high and sometimes low, sometimes loud and sometimes soft, sometimes continuous and sometimes intermittent. Sometimes it was like the sound of gold and jade clashing, sometimes like the sound of a large bell and a small bell, sometimes like large and small beads falling onto a jade plate, sometimes like red coral and white agate sinking into the sea, sometimes like playing a plain silk stringed instrument, sometimes like dancing with thunder, sometimes like a hundred birds singing in harmony, and sometimes like a rabbit falling and a hawk rising. My thoughts were racing, and I couldn't control myself. My heart was in full bloom, and the wind was blowing under my pen."}
{"trans": "There were many billboards, shops, and car horns blaring around him; he was like the man who dreamed of yellow millet in ancient legends, but he only slept for one night and didn't have that dream—instead, he felt a sense of pity. ... The Taoist walked up to a hardware store, bowed down, and of course, the store owner had no money to give him, so he just bowed his head indifferently. After getting up, he knocked on the door of the neighboring tobacco shop, and then \"fell to his knees on the dusty ground,\" his head hanging down, his movements like a black mudflow, slowly unfolding like a black chrysanthemum."}
{"trans": "So what? Birds sing in spring, crickets chirp in autumn, mosquitoes hum in summer, and at night, insects wake up while birds sleep. Rain and wind are not daily occurrences, and dogs do not bark without a reason, nor do chickens lay eggs without a purpose. Only humans use language, actions, and machines to make sounds at any time and place. Even when alone in a room with no one to respond, they can turn on a record player, listen to the radio, or even make thunder-like nasal sounds while sleeping. Of course, language is not just about sound, but in unpleasant, unwanted, or distant sounds that are not true language, words lose their edges and contours, turning into a noisy mass that swells and shrinks, lacking meaning just like a dog's bark."}
{"trans": "As time passes, the past is forever gone and cannot be brought back to the moment when the peach blossoms and the people first met; however, in people's memories, the past charm or lingering pain often resurfaces, making the present an extension of the past charm or lingering pain, and even more profound. If life is a blank book pre-bound and paginated, the disturbance of past events to people is like writing a page with too much force, causing the ink to seep into the following pages, which cannot be erased. Of course, there is no need to destroy the old pages to feel better, just like there is no need to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower after the Yellow Crane has already flown away; however, it is necessary to spread out the old history under the lamp, to act where one should act, and to stop where one should stop."}
{"trans": "The Great Northwest is a barren basalt mountain, a vast desert with a lone plume of smoke rising into the sky. You are a geologist, with a large geological satchel made of canvas slung over your shoulder, and you have been traveling for twenty years. Your tent, in the sand mountains and sea of sand, is like a small boat, with a crescent moon shining down on it. Can the bell of Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou City be heard \"at midnight on a guest ship\"? Your wife, that beautiful woman like a flower, is looking at you, her face covered in a web of longing. She is trying to retrieve a heart of love that has drifted away. You return once a year, planting a clump of bamboo in front of the door each time, but then you leave again, leaving her with the character \"个\" (ge) made of bamboo leaves."}
{"trans": "If life is a book pre-bound and paginated with blank pages, past events disturbing a person are like writing a page with too much force, causing ink to seep into the following pages, leaving indelible marks. Of course, there is no need to destroy old pages to feel better, just as there is no need to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower after the Yellow Crane has flown away. However, it is necessary to spread out the old history under the lamp, to act where one should act, and to stop where one should stop. After fully embracing life, one can tolerate and give due position and meaning to both old events and new things. If it is a beautiful thing, one can see what kind of branches grow from the buds of this event; if it is a sad thing, one can also see a tender branch stretching from the cloudy day to the sunny day."}
{"trans": "Everything felt distant from me, and even my own shadow in the moonlight seemed hazier than mist. I was about to turn around and go to sleep; somehow, I hesitated for a moment before taking a step, and my fleeting dream suddenly came to a halt, though it soon resumed its swift flight like an arrow."}
{"trans": "In the end, all that is left to hope for is an aesthetic support. It is like a ship sinking in an ice sea with no hope of rescue, looking up to see the dark clouds rolling in; it is like being surrounded by chaos with no way out, looking down to see the bloodstains on the ground. Aesthetic support is the last support."}
{"trans": "What we have gathered in the past and will gather in the future are but seeds. When you are a desire wandering in the fog, I am also wandering there. We seek each other out, and from our longing, dreams grow, dreams that are endless and boundless."}
{"trans": "In this purity, the dish is oneself, the person cooking is oneself, and the person eating is also oneself. Just as love is oneself, knowing that the one who loves is oneself, and the one who remembers this love is also oneself. One tastes oneself bite by bite, through the cup of time, and one intoxicates oneself."}
{"trans": "The trousers were tight and I couldn't lift my foot. My heart was as pure as a sheet of paper, as blank as a newborn baby. I bid farewell to the sea and to the lonely seabird soaring in the sky. I will come back to pick up the dust of the eight wildernesses and nine heavens. I picked up my umbrella and shoes, and picked up all the things of the world."}
{"trans": "It is impossible to predict. I only hope that, even as a human flaw, it will be presented in a dignified manner. Like the solemn sigh of a noble warrior, rather than the chaotic midnight brawl of a group of ragged soldiers; like the thousand-year standoff between two snow-capped peaks, rather than a tangle of wild vines wrapped around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was extremely beautiful. The sky seemed to be a blue artifact burned during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty, deep and boundless. Through the moon as large as a silver table, one could still see the metallic blue light behind the moon. The moonlight was no match for the blue sky's dyeing, and it was as if diluted ink, gradually dissipating."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie repeatedly is like spitting out food and chewing it again. For a moment, our heads turned golden, as if covered in wheat stalks. I recalled a character in Gorky's book who said that young lovers should not meet again, as if a skeleton had risen from the ground..."}
{"trans": "As soon as I close my eyes, I think of it, and as soon as I open my eyes, I want it. When all of this comes rushing at me, almost drowning me, I have no idea what I really want. I just feel my heart aching, as if it's being tightly constricted by threads of silk, scorched by drops of candle tears, and tossed about on the vast sea."}
{"trans": "The faintest echo of your sobs will become its voice. After its life is veiled, it will be as hidden and obscured as your greatest soul. When life speaks, all the winds become words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips and the tears in your eyes will also become words."}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality has become increasingly dim. With the passing of seasons, the plum blossoms wither and the cranes grow old, and culture becomes a purposeless waste, while closed moral perfection leads to overall immorality. The rapid advancement of civilization is thus canceled, leaving behind a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks, sandwiched in the annals of the national spirit."}
{"trans": "Issuing a passport to religious spirituality based on science and philosophy is like falling in love with intellect and reasoning, which inevitably suppresses the passion of life and depletes the charm of love. Replacing religious spirituality with political and economic policies is like considering family background and wealth as marriage conditions, and becoming a spiritual eunuch by sacrificing children as reproductive machines."}
{"trans": "In fact, all destruction is specific, and all grievances are inexpressible, so those answers are also questionable. What is unquestionable is the result: the decaying grass and rubble, bearing the weight of countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all of this in a perilous environment without any protective mechanism, just as I would remove my gloves to touch an old man's wounds."}
{"trans": "Now I have written many pages. I see myself as a child copying a passage from a long hymn; the angels sang that hymn when God created the first man. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person memorizing a sentence from a book written by the wise; that book was written on the title page of emotions before time began."}
{"trans": "Even the great events that span millennia, even the monumental achievements that connect distant lands, if they belong to culture, are often borne by a pair of aged shoulders. Like smugglers, like fugitives, they dodge and hide along the way, searching for a place to entrust their legacy. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, and thus it is destined that they will not live to explain the cultural significance of their lives."}
{"trans": "There is no doubt about the result: the decaying grass and rubble bear the weight of countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all of this in a perilous environment without any protective mechanism, just as I would touch an old man's scars without gloves. This kind of touch often leads to deep reflection: as the foundation of our lives, Chinese civilization is also scarred and battered, yet how has it managed to avoid a complete collapse?"}
{"trans": "Can anyone enclose the meaning of creation in a birth certificate and give it to you? Birth is inherently a request for meaning from the person being born, requiring you to seek or establish meaning, much like a publishing contract with an advance payment, with a lifetime duration. Of course, you are not the creditor but the debtor, and it is life that demands meaning from you, leaving no room for you to complain about who is to blame."}
{"trans": "The uneven ink, the overprinted headlines, the crossed-out names, the rows of exclamation marks, the timid complaints, and the repeated corrections all combined to create a terrifying sound that came rushing at us. It was as if just a few white hairs on the corner of a spider's web or a piece of torn cloth among the withered leaves at the treetops could immediately transport us back to an era we dare not think about again."}
{"trans": "Some fell onto the hair of the vegetable pickers, some stuck to the black coats of the swallows, and some slipped into the small streams to play. The river, like a thousand flute-playing vagabonds, accompanied the cheerful songs of the children leaving school. When the naughty children placed their books on their yellow hats and waded across the river with their shoes in hand, would the spore babies pop out of the flute holes, bite the children's clothes, and finally return to the soil of their wild fern mothers?"}
{"trans": "Soul, come back, and return to my old home. When he spoke in Minnan dialect and made people burst into laughter, and when he spoke in Beijing dialect and made people look at each other in confusion, why did he never defend himself: Here, his Chu accent is as profound as the mountains and rivers, and as grand as the heavens and gods? Every note from the emcee is like his father reciting the \"Chenqing Biao\", melodious and sorrowful, each note is a heavy blow to you."}
{"trans": "He was too thin, and his dry skin couldn't fill the gaps between his ribs, so the flatbread was like a steel bridge, spanning over the ribs. His strong and dull heartbeat was like a bleeding sun, burning hollowly and emitting flames and cavernous sounds. Mei Ying had heard Yue Bei's heartbeat, which was deep and low, and through his well-developed muscles, his heart beat like coal buried deep in the earth's crust, stable and rhythmic."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, never settling in a mountain village or by the water, what is the talisman I can pray for? Perhaps it is youth, but how fleeting it is. I am like a treasure hunter who carries pearls and gold and silver in a leaky bag, only to find that the weight diminishes with every step, and youth has turned to dust. Perhaps it is the scriptures and classics, but can a full belly of knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hands?"}
{"trans": "In the mountains of my hometown, greeting someone from afar is never a soft and mushy \"oh—\" like the city folks, nor a Southern accent's feigned surprise \"wow—\". The \"oh\" and \"wow\" can't travel far before being swallowed by the mountains. Only a deep, rich, long, and desolate \"uh-ha—\" can soar like an eagle for a long time. Now, this eagle's cry falls like mist from the sky, and endless homesickness fills Shen Zhanping's chest, hot and spicy."}
{"trans": "Quickly escape from the political quagmire that even I don't fully understand, and chase after the long-lost poetic feeling. Chasing after poetic feeling is also chasing after myself, the self that was once familiar to the nine provinces, the self that was held tightly by my wife, the self that I thought I had found but actually lost. This time, I am chasing back with the morning sun as my companion, the river as my witness, the sound of monkeys as my encouragement, and the mountains making way for me. Therefore, the ship of life, which was becoming heavier and heavier, has once again become a light boat."}
{"trans": "Although an airplane can be thought of as Zhuangzi's carefree journey or Liezi's wind-riding trip, it is not very interesting to watch. It is nothing like the long journey by train, with its hypnotic rhythm and ever-changing scenery seen through the window, which is both like being in the world and yet beyond it. Therefore, when traveling abroad, wherever the steady double tracks of the train can take me, I always stand on the platform—a veritable \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the train, with its masculine beauty, to rumble and continuously push into the station to take me to distant places."}
{"trans": "The confrontation with the powerful is a common occurrence, while the confrontation with the officialdom is that of the common people. The everyday life of ordinary people in a small town is more concealed than the dense reeds and trees in the mountains. The concealment in the mountains still preserves and boasts a kind of aloofness, but aloof concealment is ultimately insincere; the concealment in the small town market not only does not need to deliberately torture and destroy life, but can also make life very comfortable, allowing life to be smoothed out in a quiet and convenient corner, and can almost dissolve itself from the outside to the inside, thus becoming the highest form of concealment. Saying concealment is perhaps too narrow-minded, but in my mind, the small bridge, flowing water, and the homesickness for freshwater fish are all ecological images of a religious philosophy of life."}
